// The one place the shv2 query spine's hashing carries policy; the fold itself is `stdlib/Hasher`.
//
// Every per-file query (queryTokens, queryParseOps) is keyed on the content hash of its input, and
// the whole-program queryAllModule is keyed on a composite hash folded over every file's content
// hash in source-path order. Content-hash keying is **parallel-safe**: a hash is computed
// independently per file with no shared mutable state, so per-file parse tasks never contend on a
// global counter, and two builds of byte-identical input produce byte-identical cache keys.

// Fold a byte sequence into a running hash, tagged with its length.
//
// The tag is the policy: FNV-1a folds a flat byte sequence, so without a length "ab" then "c" and
// "a" then "bc" reach one digest — and the signature index folds a name, then a return type, then
// the next name. It lives here rather than in stdlib because anything that must interoperate with
// another FNV-1a implementation needs the bare fold.
//
// Takes a `ByteArray`, so a caller that already holds one — every interned name is a zero-copy
// slice of the source — hashes it without building a String.
export function mixBytes(state HashDigest, bytes ByteArray) returns HashDigest
	return Hasher.combined(Hasher.combined(state, bytes: bytes), value: bytes.count())
end 'mixBytes'
